END
The main concept to remember

There are three important parts in this program:

1. Input section
List<Integer> a = new ArrayList<>();

and

List<Integer> b = new ArrayList<>();

These create the two lists.

2. Processing section
for (int i = 0; i < a.size(); i++) {
    if (a.get(i) > b.get(i)) {
        Alice_score++;
    }
    else if (a.get(i) < b.get(i)) {
        Bob_score++;
    }
}

This is where the actual problem-solving happens.

3. Return section
scores.add(Alice_score);
scores.add(Bob_score);

return scores;

This creates:

[Alice score, Bob score]

and sends it back to main().
